#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124320 :question/id #uuid "266a9a4e-cb11-5e4a-a2ac-c2e734966372" :question/math-academy-id "e-5424" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4 \\times 4$ matrix, and \n![](images/6a/6a294de4a5f2ff5755d8ceb5b91bb8920685a1cf2b5e727c5b5fdcfaaf0b89b0.svg)\n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\textrm{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^4$\n\nIII. $\\textrm{rank}(A)=4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4 \\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following: \n\n![](images/4b/4b42fd4ec8ccf491a1244a648af6fe40ce846fad388685e36d499783a095f8f7.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since \n![](images/32/327a582d15b82ebccda48358062310e6ad5c3bb2689f2024d76a8f8e7e1401a0.svg)\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1 \\neq 0.\n$$\n\nSo,  according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since the matrix $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\textrm{Col}(A) \\neq \\mathbb{R}^4.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\textrm{rank}(A) \\neq 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519985 :question-generator/id #uuid "2c8a204b-6657-54da-84cb-6832f441443e" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124511.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "235a52da-656a-5cf2-a401-0f42a3642391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459823} {:answer/id #uuid "04790f9e-17da-5ed1-82d4-a7391bccbd0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "235a52da-656a-5cf2-a401-0f42a3642391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459823} :answer-field/id #uuid "419ff1b3-8e47-5988-b4a7-49adadda7718" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e39055a2-7be3-5968-8135-398e60211c8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459825} {:answer/id #uuid "f28e5027-719a-5804-a84a-81f68d441b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f28e5027-719a-5804-a84a-81f68d441b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459826} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6ef0960-7c5f-543c-a81b-bf7733be9b0f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3932a553-bb8b-5851-b93b-ecabd828b7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459827} {:answer/id #uuid "909e13f6-b658-585b-af87-0fb072eb5e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3932a553-bb8b-5851-b93b-ecabd828b7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459827} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c740ae4-9a04-5de5-a467-c4e121394796" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460780}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5b63a26-4713-5ecd-9d64-befaccc0bd77" :question/math-academy-id "q-34834" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n\nII. $A$ is not invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=5$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9128cbd6-bc0c-595b-a248-301d01f8b7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121821} {:answer/id #uuid "efc1e85a-3284-5066-834c-a323d5c71513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121822} {:answer/id #uuid "f5bd34c7-b021-5e08-821f-eda58f26af49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121823} {:answer/id #uuid "f62e59b1-d023-55b4-8ab1-2cd64802f471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121824} {:answer/id #uuid "3284bcfa-ffff-5fae-8659-11357928e9c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121825}] :answer-field/id #uuid "828bb6eb-1fea-579c-aa5b-35f52ffd61b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121820}] :question/id #uuid "c1c9e6d5-730c-5efc-93c4-7ddaee4eba06" :question/math-academy-id "q-34936" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6 \\cdot 6$ matrix and $Col(A) = R^{6}$?\n\n1. $A$ is not invertible\n2. $rank(A) = 6$\n3. $dim(Null(A)) = 6$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c0a6001-3780-5910-af1b-80f1dc86bb46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449628} {:answer/id #uuid "711f6d61-9af9-514f-ab7b-3f6b87059a2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c0a6001-3780-5910-af1b-80f1dc86bb46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449628} :answer-field/id #uuid "577301d3-bda4-5711-b8ea-c8d7c59e3764" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fd05ec0-7412-5317-bd1f-6fdd48ffae9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449630} {:answer/id #uuid "7e775f74-22c8-5e41-92ca-9b7679c5d763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e775f74-22c8-5e41-92ca-9b7679c5d763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449631} :answer-field/id #uuid "11747fa2-61fa-56a5-ab66-ef191899dff3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17f12245-1e0f-5cf0-8c20-1a321c65854b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449632} {:answer/id #uuid "2e93e8a1-abd3-5bae-8c25-a6156dc77f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e93e8a1-abd3-5bae-8c25-a6156dc77f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449633} :answer-field/id #uuid "71691d56-9200-5496-becc-0f211d28a39b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450770}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f63719f4-7a1e-5b43-8302-7786de4d0619" :question/math-academy-id "q-141199" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{Null}(A)={0}$\n- **II.** $A$ is not invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne {0},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f87f060-5b8c-5b4a-806f-8cf93ee4d70d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449634} {:answer/id #uuid "4360a160-1403-523e-8e62-4fbb2ec722d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4360a160-1403-523e-8e62-4fbb2ec722d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449635} :answer-field/id #uuid "359ebe96-94aa-58ea-b60b-be863ac84a52" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb552ac2-1033-5cf0-95e3-c64844f7abfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449636} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cf0040-9b44-519e-ab54-532b2b101a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0cf0040-9b44-519e-ab54-532b2b101a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449637} :answer-field/id #uuid "65159a93-fba0-5a45-abcc-86fe85e1adb6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39e5820e-dedb-509b-bef8-5b24f4aea7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449638} {:answer/id #uuid "319a4d81-4806-58b2-9a6b-94494e8c5b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39e5820e-dedb-509b-bef8-5b24f4aea7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449638} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8aa8650-12f8-56c0-ac84-85ed73892db0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450773}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dad0d98-37c5-5af9-9c0a-4f0fabec2bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-141200" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is invertible\n\n- **II.** $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(A)=6$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f8d9af-560e-5e04-801f-49c3569ea09a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464240} {:answer/id #uuid "3683cdbb-cea0-5d3a-88ae-46bbf35523a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07f8d9af-560e-5e04-801f-49c3569ea09a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464240} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8b8cb5-e75e-518a-91a0-160dae2c2bc4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bba33a3-e841-5573-8abf-90651ed20a6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464242} {:answer/id #uuid "0c34db9f-4df3-5319-9c26-896a5b27e435" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bba33a3-e841-5573-8abf-90651ed20a6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464242} :answer-field/id #uuid "05d917c1-327f-5ee0-8aed-ef99e81a107b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de2f17c6-86e7-560e-b3af-0ab0f7aab9fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464244} {:answer/id #uuid "06de2a3a-d315-52ff-898b-03d434ea28ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06de2a3a-d315-52ff-898b-03d434ea28ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464245} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bcd47e5-e550-5069-9017-2362f6f7a623" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465056}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c320bbb-0961-56b0-99e4-beaa75aa8f10" :question/math-academy-id "q-142358" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}?\n$$\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n- **II.** $A$ is  invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4ec697a-de36-58b0-a09b-ffb9c847aeff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449652} {:answer/id #uuid "78fdbd67-166e-573c-b77c-2875405073f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4ec697a-de36-58b0-a09b-ffb9c847aeff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449652} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4acbd25-fc0e-5df4-a5a0-9e2908a9bffc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb540fd1-edb6-5d6c-ba67-f5731cd79a1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449654} {:answer/id #uuid "436ef14f-26d4-5b22-b36f-ed6da6246439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb540fd1-edb6-5d6c-ba67-f5731cd79a1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449654} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c9e25d7-83f7-5d4a-9ef5-64e221fc60a5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5d749ec-8e32-58f1-997a-3d7c01f317b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449656} {:answer/id #uuid "93874984-dcb6-5b93-8915-727ca84b807f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93874984-dcb6-5b93-8915-727ca84b807f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449657} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1cc353b-858d-567c-919c-e053dd74f9d8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450782}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4927fd87-c83e-52d3-b9bb-877110a8c514" :question/math-academy-id "q-142474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ccb0567-0495-5c74-8699-bab086a64809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450560} {:answer/id #uuid "62954330-fa79-5088-bd4b-cb797b88fe25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ccb0567-0495-5c74-8699-bab086a64809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450560} :answer-field/id #uuid "c34e741f-afd5-539e-89ed-87f3b75f5ff9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46523043-bc55-5cb6-b33f-a37a5b648d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450562} {:answer/id #uuid "2d38beb7-b0db-523b-99bb-2bb27ec73198" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46523043-bc55-5cb6-b33f-a37a5b648d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450562} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46ab9df-f1e2-5ca8-bca4-a8a7559c9764" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd58a89b-6f9b-54a1-881b-e354c7de0b9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450564} {:answer/id #uuid "2d103fe3-6dbf-53c9-a8ce-da05a06b3a9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d103fe3-6dbf-53c9-a8ce-da05a06b3a9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450565} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f8121ca-3a46-557f-84a4-3de651e3583d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451236}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9288acd6-ddf2-55d8-ba92-e1c27cfdfe7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-35425" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$  is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426076 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13e3d0a6-c269-5dde-bafd-a91861927c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426036} {:answer/id #uuid "1848f756-51a0-5639-8084-5aa59abdaebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426037} {:answer/id #uuid "562361ed-d031-5fb2-9175-4571a3994648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426047} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7285e7-4a5d-5073-aa0f-ffd3853ddc65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "lI only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426054} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d58843-37c3-5988-8dac-72db97dcd1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d58843-37c3-5988-8dac-72db97dcd1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426064} :answer-field/id #uuid "fec9750c-eaeb-571d-b465-6fa1ab05e88d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426071}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fbccd10-1c43-51a4-ad8b-36063e11427d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142367" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$  is  invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2024e7-8603-5e5a-8b2e-7cb9aa759b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453380} {:answer/id #uuid "83ac7d4b-d4c5-5c92-8589-e7ec5bddcb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83ac7d4b-d4c5-5c92-8589-e7ec5bddcb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453381} :answer-field/id #uuid "89392c96-2fc2-5a4d-8885-bb32eafcba1e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454440} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79098b74-c172-54b9-82e2-49824d97c9bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453382} {:answer/id #uuid "0ffeb813-fd36-5776-8ba7-23c839dba453" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79098b74-c172-54b9-82e2-49824d97c9bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453382} :answer-field/id #uuid "be118244-9178-534b-8fc7-3f7c4f68e4fc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454441} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05113400-1012-5e94-b50e-c93f67bd0a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453384} {:answer/id #uuid "75b2fb9a-b3d9-55ad-8209-77f57b32b7e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75b2fb9a-b3d9-55ad-8209-77f57b32b7e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453385} :answer-field/id #uuid "994ca1fa-debf-5f93-b9db-34b6b1ce3215" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454442}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0f098cb-e297-54fe-a435-e8a16d43aa06" :question/math-academy-id "q-139977" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2b28520-430a-5247-a200-fd5f414e5ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454012} {:answer/id #uuid "f8033251-ab93-5bb9-a145-e5e99be3d388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2b28520-430a-5247-a200-fd5f414e5ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454012} :answer-field/id #uuid "da3c91e0-c158-561e-ab32-6e72b9ba78b5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "647ee441-bfd6-5c35-84c4-0fc1e7479328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454014} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e66778-9876-5718-a6e2-1e95fc527bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "647ee441-bfd6-5c35-84c4-0fc1e7479328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454014} :answer-field/id #uuid "030534f1-c9cc-5372-9ff2-bdc749c441e3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31d47ce5-4beb-5f68-bae7-0d361ea95c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454016} {:answer/id #uuid "f6dcdf0f-841a-5b0d-aff9-db735d828b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6dcdf0f-841a-5b0d-aff9-db735d828b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454017} :answer-field/id #uuid "eced16f4-9e93-50d2-bf88-cdda3960f7ec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454758}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea4581af-a083-51da-803f-0f83b3ed2ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-79349" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is not invertible\n\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\n- **III.** $A$ has $5$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=5$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446312} {:answer/id #uuid "2dee1bb0-b584-5a13-acb7-dbc8b8f98b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446317} {:answer/id #uuid "a01f5c26-889c-59f3-aea4-5b800234178a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446339} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fd3f74-8d86-59d5-969d-0f73063566e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446345} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a5d0c5-12bc-5492-a130-1c6bfb4dadcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446312} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b91479d-fc9f-5493-8022-99b07638d6b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446361}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "007b2eff-be4f-5ff5-af75-29d7ce49d108" :question/math-academy-id "q-141201" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and  $\\text{rank}(A)=4?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ is an invertible matrix because $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is invertible, it must be $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$ because $A$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5602a65b-5713-5ed2-bdd4-7c2a89efe1f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446321} {:answer/id #uuid "6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446329} {:answer/id #uuid "8d75866b-a6fe-5c0e-8c96-11f1e0e723da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446336} {:answer/id #uuid "f63ddbaf-3159-5f89-a08c-517e465848a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446357} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7d54d8-0b88-5b60-9559-438bba9408ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446329} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a8a987-b1f9-5fda-b11d-202fd35c0139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446365}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a0c9232-89fc-57dc-83d9-632995f2a765" :question/math-academy-id "q-34929" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83819081-3ffe-5b21-ac5b-ef6bd26bb168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446333} {:answer/id #uuid "8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446334} {:answer/id #uuid "86f2e9f4-3420-54d6-a57c-2966d7bea624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446335} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dd8b94-5449-5e15-bbed-68d5ef48c3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446341} {:answer/id #uuid "f453a8ad-b614-59d8-8bdc-cf9373db8c89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446334} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78aa62f-0e43-5933-85ca-b11f30121e9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446368}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40fb1ecb-b40f-5f25-b77a-57f70d15c44b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141198" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=0?$ \n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col)}(A)=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null)}(A)=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. A matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=0,$ our matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\nSince $A$ is not invertible, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible,  it must be $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446314} {:answer/id #uuid "76cde27a-9ace-54a5-8396-92267ce3cc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446332} {:answer/id #uuid "9adf27f7-10ea-578a-a1d6-83396d7db9c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446338} {:answer/id #uuid "f550b866-e3d0-5255-9950-2dbd691d15a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446356} {:answer/id #uuid "f97850ab-a157-554f-a1df-1ca38933ab0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446314} :answer-field/id #uuid "33cd506b-d09b-50d0-b353-d0e67be14e46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446364}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66aeec20-f33b-58e9-909c-e866d7b79c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-141196" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}]}
